            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Specific features of most common arrhythmias and cardiac conduction disorders found in patients with acute coronary syndrome are described. The review is intended for physicians properly informed on the general principles of the diagnosis and treatment of cardiac arrhythmias, as a differentiated concise guideline on approaching these patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
